IC) to a Photon OS instance. The error text returned by Vagrant is:\n\n``` bash\nbash: line 2: awk: command not found\nThe following SSH command responded with a non-zero exit status.\nVagrant assumes that this means the command failed!\n\nmv /tmp/bash: line 2: awk: command not found /etc/systemd/network/\n\nStdout from the command:\n\n\n\nStderr from the command:\n\nmv: cannot stat '/tmp/bash:': No such file or directory\nmv: cannot stat 'line': No such file or directory\nmv: cannot stat '2:': No such file or directory\nmv: cannot stat 'awk:': No such file or directory\nmv: cannot stat 'command': No such file or directory\nmv: cannot stat 'not': No such file or directory\nmv: cannot stat 'found': No such file or directory\n```\n\nI've also updated the vagrant-guests-photon plugin to v1.0.4, but the error persists. The only way around the error (that I've found so far) is to only use a single NIC.\n\nMore information:\nHost OS = OS X 10.11.5\nVagrant version = 1.8.5\nVirtualBox version = 5.1.4\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vmware/photon/issues/537/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vmware/photon/issues/537/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":815355085,"node_id":"MDE1OlJlZmVyZW5jZWRFdmVudDgxNTM1NTA4NQ==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hashicorp/vagrant/issues/events/815355085","actor":{"login":"markpeek","id":638982,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzODk4Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/638982?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/markpeek","html_url":"https://github.com/markpeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markpeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markpeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markpeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.c